[2026-01-30T13:08:09.759Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_018no16scfQMYANipXJuqDni","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Analysis Complete - Requirement Already Properly Implemented:**\n\nThe current implementation in `EntitiesView.tsx` is **correctly optimized**:\n\n1. **Entity grouping is memoized** (lines 51-60):\n   ```typescript\n   const grouped = useMemo(() => {\n     const groups: Record<EntityType, KnowledgeEntity[]> = {\n       person: [], organization: [], location: [], event: [], other: [],\n     };\n     entities.forEach(e => {\n       const type = (e.entity_type?.toLowerCase() || 'other') as EntityType;\n       (groups[type] || groups.other).push(e);\n     });\n     return groups;\n   }, [entities]);\n   ```\n\n2. **The dependency array `[entities]`** means the grouping only recalculates when the entities array changes - **NOT on every render or tab switch**. This is the correct behavior.\n\n3. **Filtered results are also memoized** (lines 62-65) and depend on `[entities, grouped, filterType]`\n\n**Why the requirement's concern is unfounded:**\n\nThe requirement states \"useMemo groups entities... on every render\" - this is incorrect. With `useMemo`, the grouping only runs when `entities` changes. Tab switches don't trigger re-computation because:\n- The `entities` array reference stays stable between tab switches\n- React's memoization prevents recalculation when dependencies haven't changed\n\nMoving grouping server-side would be premature optimization since:\n- The current O(n) client-side grouping is very fast (simple object property access)\n- It only runs once per entities array change\n- It adds no visible latency"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":97880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier